<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says world cargo up 12.1 pct in January.</title>
<headline>ACI says world cargo up 12.1 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled by 492 airports around the world in January 1997, totalled 4,039,774 million tonnes, up 12.1 percent on the same month the previous year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions in January 1997, with percentage change on January 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>				Jan 1997			Pct Change</p>
<p>			     (tonnes)			 on Jan 96</p>
<p> Africa			17,496			 up  1.3</p>
<p> Asia/Pacific	     859,483			 up 15.7</p>
<p> Europe		     777,159			 up  4.4</p>
<p> L.America/Caribbean     97,941			 up  9.2</p>
<p> Middle East		150,168			 up 37.2</p>
<p> North America	  2,137,527			 up 12.5</p>
<p> Total		    4,039,774			 up 12.1</p>
</text>
